  ('The Legend of John Maynard Memorial', 'the-legend-of-john-maynard-memorial', 'folklore', 42.880979, -78.888742, 'Buffalo', 'NY', 'A four-foot plaque at the Erie Basin Marina commemorating Theodor Fontane''s poem about a helmsman who steers a burning Lake Erie steamer to shore. Maynard is a fictionalised name over a real rescue. Buffalo and its German sister city Dortmund dedicated it in 1997, with the finished plaque rededicated in 1998.', 'open', null, 'http://www.johnmaynard.net/mem.html', '2026-09-06T22:43:52.581802+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('The Legend of the Iron Hoop', 'the-legend-of-the-iron-hoop', 'folklore', 41.145601, -81.339982, 'Kent', 'OH', 'A five-piece outdoor sculpture by Brinsley Tyrrell, professor emeritus at Kent State, made in 1980-81 and inspired by twisted dry wood near his home. After stints elsewhere in Ohio it was installed permanently near Henderson Hall in July 2011.', 'open', null, 'https://www.kent.edu/universityarchitect/sculptures-loan-ohio-arts-council', '2026-09-06T22:43:52.581802+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
